1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,406
Footsteps on the stairs, in the middle of

2
00:00:02,416 --> 00:00:02,751
the night.

3
00:00:02,981 --> 00:00:05,082
That's what a former curator reported at

4
00:00:05,092 --> 00:00:06,953
the White River Light Station, near

5
00:00:06,963 --> 00:00:08,064
Whitehall, Michigan.

6
00:00:08,614 --> 00:00:11,922
The lighthouse was built in 1875 and first

7
00:00:11,932 --> 00:00:14,036
lit in May 1876.

8
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:16,084
Its first keeper was Captain William

9
00:00:16,094 --> 00:00:18,086
Robinson, who came from England.

10
00:00:18,536 --> 00:00:20,941
He and his wife, Sarah, had 13 children.

11
00:00:21,171 --> 00:00:23,278
He kept the light for more than 40 years.

12
00:00:23,728 --> 00:00:27,524
In 1919, at 87, he was retired, and his

13
00:00:27,534 --> 00:00:29,051
grandson took over as keeper.

14
00:00:29,281 --> 00:00:31,437
That same spring, the old captain died.

15
00:00:32,187 --> 00:00:33,686
People say he never left.

16
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:36,101
Guests and staff have reported footsteps

17
00:00:36,111 --> 00:00:38,008
upstairs, and the tap of a cane.

18
00:00:38,658 --> 00:00:40,675
The light was shut off in 1960.

19
00:00:40,905 --> 00:00:43,447
Since 1970, it has been a museum.

20
00:00:43,897 --> 00:00:45,940
Comment your town, and it could be next.

